# Slim the build context. frontend/ didn't have this file, so every docker build sent the whole directory
# to the daemon -- 513M locally (node_modules 468M), and on the deploy machine all the past dist.bak backups.
#
# node_modules especially is pointless: the image does `COPY package*.json` + `npm ci` to reinstall,
# so the host's copy is **never used** and just gets sent for nothing.

node_modules/
.npm/

# Build output and past backups. dist.bak.* is left by the deploy script, 11M each time;
# without excluding it, "the more deploys, the slower the next build".
dist/
dist.new/
dist.bak.*/
stats.html

# Local environment and caches
.env
.env.*
.vite/
*.log
coverage/
